#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:5
msgid "Preferred CPUs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:7
msgid ""
"In paravirtualized environments CPU overcommit is a common scenario. i.e. "
"the sum of virtual CPUs (vCPUs) of all VMs is greater than number of "
"physical CPUs (pCPUs). Under such conditions when all or many VMs have high "
"utilization, hypervisor won't be able to satisfy the CPU requirement and has "
"to context switch within or across VMs. The hypervisor needs to preempt one "
"vCPU to run another. This is called vCPU preemption. This is more expensive "
"compared to task context switch within a vCPU, since hypervisor lacks vCPU "
"context and could preempt a critical section which slows forward progress."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:17
msgid ""
"In such cases it is better that combined vCPU demand from all VMs is reduced "
"by not using some of the vCPUs in each VM. vCPUs where workload can be "
"safely scheduled which won't increase any contention for pCPU are called "
"\"Preferred CPUs\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:22
msgid ""
"One of the main design constructs is that preferred CPUs are always a subset "
"of active CPUs. In most cases preferred CPUs will be same as active CPUs. "
"When there is pCPU contention, Preferred CPUs will reduce based on the steal "
"time. When the pCPU contention goes away as indicated by steal time, "
"Preferred CPUs could become same as active CPUs again. The policy decisions "
"are to be taken by driver. For example, steal_governor. Look at its "
"documentation for more details. (``drivers/virt/steal_governor.c``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:31
msgid ""
"Scheduling decisions such as wakeup, pushing the task etc, need this CPU "
"state info. This is maintained in ``cpu_preferred_mask``. vCPUs which are "
"not in ``cpu_preferred_mask`` should be treated as vCPUs which should not be "
"used at this moment provided it doesn't break user affinity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:36
msgid "This is achieved by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:38
msgid "Selecting a preferred CPU at wakeup using fallback mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:39
msgid "Pushing the task away from non-preferred CPU at tick."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:40
msgid "Selecting only preferred CPUs for load balance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:42
msgid ""
"``/sys/devices/system/cpu/preferred`` prints the current "
"``cpu_preferred_mask`` in cpulist format."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:45
msgid "Notes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:47
msgid ""
"This feature is available under ``CONFIG_PREFERRED_CPU``. Driver which makes "
"decisions should enable it. For example, steal_governor driver "
"(``CONFIG_STEAL_GOVERNOR``). On enabling the driver, CPU preferred state can "
"change based on steal time. Without the driver, preferred CPUs is same as "
"active CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:53
msgid "This feature works for the FAIR class only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:55
msgid ""
"A pinned task, which can't be moved to preferred CPUs will continue to run "
"based on its affinity. But no load balancing happens if it is affined only "
"on non-preferred CPUs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:59
msgid ""
"Decision to change the preferred CPU state is driven by the kernel. Hence it "
"shouldn't break user affinities. One of the main reasons why CPU hotplug or "
"Isolated cpuset partitions was not a solution."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../scheduler/sched-paravirt.rst:63
msgid ""
"This feature works best only when all the Guest VMs enable the feature as it "
"is a co-operative scheme. If a specific VM doesn't enable this feature it "
"may end up with more CPUs than others, still should lead to better "
"performance when seen from system view. Users who enable this driver must "
"ensure it is enabled in all Guest VMs."
msgstr ""
